COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from BU539177.1, BC017671.1 and
            AF022116.1.
            
            On Nov 22, 2018 this sequence version replaced NM_006253.4.
            
            Summary: The protein encoded by this gene is a regulatory subunit
            of the AMP-activated protein kinase (AMPK). AMPK is a heterotrimer
            consisting of an alpha catalytic subunit, and non-catalytic beta
            and gamma subunits. AMPK is an important energy-sensing enzyme that
            monitors cellular energy status. In response to cellular metabolic
            stresses, AMPK is activated, and thus phosphorylates and
            inactivates acetyl-CoA carboxylase (ACC) and beta-hydroxy
            beta-methylglutaryl-CoA reductase (HMGCR), key enzymes involved in
            regulating de novo biosynthesis of fatty acid and cholesterol. This
            subunit may be a positive regulator of AMPK activity. The
            myristoylation and phosphorylation of this subunit have been shown
            to affect the enzyme activity and cellular localization of AMPK.
            This subunit may also serve as an adaptor molecule mediating the
            association of the AMPK complex. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
