   PUBMED   34978780
COMMENT     REVIEWED REFSEQ: This record has been curated by NCBI staff. The
            reference sequence was derived from AC127430.4, DA800082.1,
            BX649110.1, AK127782.1, BC117162.1, AY576987.1, AI671342.1 and
            AC094020.2.
            
            On Feb 25, 2020 this sequence version replaced NM_014159.6.
            
            Summary: Huntington's disease (HD), a neurodegenerative disorder
            characterized by loss of striatal neurons, is caused by an
            expansion of a polyglutamine tract in the HD protein huntingtin.
            This gene encodes a protein belonging to a class of huntingtin
            interacting proteins characterized by WW motifs. This protein is a
            histone methyltransferase that is specific for lysine-36 of histone
            H3, and methylation of this residue is associated with active
            chromatin. This protein also contains a novel transcriptional
            activation domain and has been found associated with
            hyperphosphorylated RNA polymerase II. [provided by RefSeq, Aug
            2008].
            
            Transcript Variant: This variant (1) encodes the longer isoform
            (1).
            
            Publication Note:  This RefSeq record includes a subset of the
            publications that are available for this gene. Please see the Gene
            record to access additional publications.
            
